Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── Afterwards: the valley, come back to ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The book closes on the Working Day, and the valley goes on: a company that comes back finds it as the day left it.
  Chapter ch_after_seventh "Monday, and After" when pastThree() and inLull(party) and outcomeSeventh(lull_country) "The road goes down from the stone every day now, and on six of them Linger works, badly and with enormous interest, like a town that has been given a new toy; and on the seventh it rests, and the law holds, and at the Watching some things come apart and most do not. There are people in Linger under fifty-seven who have now seen a Tuesday, and talk about it.".
  Chapter ch_after_monday "A Valley Like Any Other" when pastThree() and inLull(party) and outcomeMonday(lull_country) "The road goes down from the stone every day now, and nothing in the valley comes apart at sunset any more, and nothing holds better than it would anywhere else. There is a sound from the Mill, by day, that the Old Shift do not talk about.".
  Chapter ch_after_sunday "Still Lullday" when pastThree() and inLull(party) and (outcomeSunday(lull_country) or outcomeBroken(lull_country) or outcomeMeant(lull_country)) "It is Lullday. It is always Lullday. The town is a week older than the last time you saw it, which is to say a day.".

  Observe bridge_built at mill_bridge when lullOpen() and bridgeBuilt(club) "The Shift Bridge goes over the mill-leat again: new oak on the old piers, a little crooked in the middle where Davy Mote set it, and worn already on the boards where people walk out to the middle to stand and look at the Mill.".
  Observe bridge_built_seventh at mill_bridge as feature when lullOpen() and outcomeSeventh(lull_country) "At the Mill end an old weighbridge house has a new door, and a clock over it, and a board: C. LINDSELL, CLOCKS, FOR WAGES SIX DAYS IN SEVEN.".
  Observe yard_monday at mill_yard when lullOpen() and lawGone(lull_country) and not dark() "The great doors of the Mill stand open on the yard. Inside, on the ground floor, Haskett's men are taking the warps off the old looms and stringing new ones, and a few Lull-born are watching them, and one or two are helping, carefully, the way you help with something you might be blamed for.".
  Observe stone_after at fold_stone as feature when weekReturned(lull_country) "Under all the rows of seven on the Fold-stone somebody has carved, deep: AND THEN MONDAY.".
  Observe board_week at sx_street as feature when weekReturned(lull_country) and not lawGone(lull_country) and not dark() "Somebody has rubbed the count off the board by the pump and chalked instead: LULL EVERY DAY. LULLDAY: MIND WHAT YOU MEAN.".
  Observe board_monday at sx_street as feature when lawGone(lull_country) and not dark() "The board by the pump says, in fresh chalk: LINGER, CARTING WANTED, APPLY HASKETT.".
  Observe green_week_evening at green when lullOpen() and not lawDay() and weekReturned(lull_country) and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 21 "The Long Table is laid, the way it always was, and the town eats at it, the way it always did; and nobody sets anything out on the grass, because nothing is going to come apart tonight, and the starlings go over the Tump as they always have, and nobody watches them.".
  // Where people are, afterwards.
  Rule after_tobias when outcomeSeventh(lull_country) and pastThree() and dayAt(tobias, hester_room) { Retract dayAt(tobias, hester_room). Assert dayAt(tobias, mill_bridge). Retract held(tobias). }
  Rule after_corin when (outcomeSeventh(lull_country) or outcomeSunday(lull_country)) and pastThree() and held(corin) { Retract held(corin). Retract held(club). Retract held(davy). Retract held(kezia). Retract held(piran). Retract held(aldith). Retract held(linnet). Retract held(folk). Retract held(wardens). Retract held(hobday). }
  Rule after_release when (outcomeMonday(lull_country) or outcomeBroken(lull_country)) and pastThree() and held(corin) { Retract held(corin). Retract held(club). Retract held(davy). Retract held(kezia). Retract held(piran). Retract held(aldith). Retract held(linnet). Retract held(folk). Retract held(wardens). Retract held(hobday). Retract held(tobias). }
  Observe tobias_at_bridge at mill_bridge as sign when lullOpen() and at(tobias, mill_bridge) and pastThree() "Tobias Lindsell sits on a kitchen chair at the Mill end of the bridge with a little clock ticking in his waistcoat pocket, telling the strike to a child, from the inside of the window.".
  Topic tobias_after with tobias "Ask Tobias Lindsell how he finds Monday" when pastThree() and outcomeSeventh(lull_country) and lullOpen() once {
    Says "Tobias considers it, the way he considers everything, as if it might be a trick question. 'Loud,' he says. 'Corin's hammering from six. Davy Mote has joined the Wardens, the new ones, that keep the peace on the six days and leave it alone on the seventh; he has a hat.' He takes out the little clock and looks at it. 'I am two days older than I was last Lullday. I can feel both of them.' He puts the clock away. 'Hester would have liked it. Or she'll like it, I should say, if you're asking her; she's on the bank most afternoons, telling them they're doing it wrong.'".
  }
  Topic corin_after with corin "Ask Corin Lindsell what she is making" when pastThree() and lullOpen() and (outcomeSeventh(lull_country) or outcomeSunday(lull_country)) once {
    Says "Corin holds up something small and brass, and squints at you through it. 'A clock that keeps both,' she says. 'The world's days, and the Lull's. For the stone. So Sixways can stop notching.' She turns it in the light. 'It'll come apart at sunset, I expect, the first time. I'm making it for wages, Haskett's paying.' She grins. 'And then I'll make it again for nobody, for the stone, and that one'll hold.'".
  }
}
